WEBVTT

1
00:00:00.680 --> 00:00:04.900
So what’s the most important thing you want people to remember about Mossville?

2
00:00:04.900 --> 00:00:05.460
It’s funny.

3
00:00:05.460 --> 00:00:11.200
They talk about a lot of . . . How the plants made people sick and all that,

4
00:00:11.200 --> 00:00:15.820
but these people persevered through all that and they still here.

5
00:00:15.820 --> 00:00:17.320
It was a nice place at the time.

6
00:00:17.320 --> 00:00:21.200
It was a lot of good memories for me.

7
00:00:21.200 --> 00:00:25.320
But as time change, people change, things change.

8
00:00:25.320 --> 00:00:30.640
So I’m glad y’all doing this so y’all can have some kind of history and remember.

9
00:00:30.640 --> 00:00:37.706
Because when the town goes and the people get old, any memory or record of us will be gone, so . . .

10
00:00:37.706 --> 00:00:38.300
Yeah.

11
00:00:38.300 --> 00:00:43.200
You’re the first one that we’ve interviewed that actually has mentioned how people started to get sick.

12
00:00:43.200 --> 00:00:46.740
Is that just something that folks just don’t talk about anymore?

13
00:00:46.740 --> 00:00:55.680
Well it’s a known fact around here that people of Mossville been fighting . . . fighting about these plants for years, and years, and years.

14
00:00:55.680 --> 00:00:59.500
They bought up the houses to the railroad tracks right here to the start of Mossville.

15
00:00:59.500 --> 00:01:03.200
And it’s funny a lot of people was upset because they like, “Well if this place was here,

16
00:01:03.200 --> 00:01:07.740
why . . .” I’m pretty sure water travel made . . . got in they water.

17
00:01:07.740 --> 00:01:14.380
It should have passed on, but it’s . . . People got they own reasons behind why they did what they did.

18
00:01:14.380 --> 00:01:18.160
Like I say, it’s a known fact a lot of people around here died of cancer.

19
00:01:18.160 --> 00:01:20.740
A lot of people got sick.

20
00:01:20.740 --> 00:01:28.560
But . . . and that these people in this area been fighting with the government and these plants for as long as I can remember about that.

21
00:01:28.560 --> 00:01:29.620
I am not a scientist.

22
00:01:29.620 --> 00:01:33.680
I don’t know, but what goes on speaks for itself.

23
00:01:33.680 --> 00:01:38.460
If you got a lot of people in one area getting sick then there’s something wrong.

24
00:01:38.460 --> 00:01:41.480
A lot of people around here can’t afford to . . . Couldn’t afford to leave.

25
00:01:41.480 --> 00:01:49.080
So what Sasol did helped some of the people out, but in general you have to talk to mainly the older generation about that.
